{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `marr`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `marr_safestan_copy`, a deterministic copy of `marr`, because protected data are used in `transformed data` to compute release totals before the likelihood observation. The protected likelihood was changed from a loop over indexed rows, `marr[t] ~ multinomial(pr[t])`, to the equivalent vectorized built-in statement `marr ~ multinomial(pr)` so that the protected variable appears exactly once on the left side as a plain top-level identifier. Added explicit `uniform(0, 1)` priors for `phi` and `p`, which are density-neutral for parameters already constrained to `[0, 1]` and satisfy SafeStan's unique-prior requirement. Generated-quantities fit calculations read the deterministic copy of `marr`.

Deterministic data augmentation: `marr_safestan_copy` is exactly equal to `marr` from the supplied data.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> n_occasions; // Number of capture occasions
  array[n_occasions - 1, n_occasions] int<lower=0> marr; // m-array
  array[n_occasions - 1, n_occasions] int<lower=0> marr_safestan_copy; // deterministic copy of marr for pre-observation use
}
transformed data {
  // Compoud declaration was enabled in Stan 2.13
  int n_occasions_minus_1 = n_occasions - 1;
  //  int n_occasions_minus_1;
  array[n_occasions - 1] int r;

  //  n_occasions_minus_1 = n_occasions - 1;

  // Calculate the number of birds released each year
  for (t in 1 : n_occasions_minus_1) {
    r[t] = sum(marr_safestan_copy[t]);
  }
}
parameters {
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[n_occasions_minus_1] phi; // Survival
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[n_occasions_minus_1] p; // Recapture
}
transformed parameters {
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[n_occasions_minus_1] q;
  array[n_occasions_minus_1] simplex[n_occasions] pr;

  q = 1.0 - p; // Probability of non-recapture

  // Define the cell probabilities of the m-array
  for (t in 1 : n_occasions_minus_1) {
    // Main diagonal
    pr[t, t] = phi[t] * p[t];

    // Above main diagonal
    for (j in (t + 1) : n_occasions_minus_1) {
      pr[t, j] = prod(phi[t : j]) * prod(q[t : (j - 1)]) * p[j];
    }

    // Below main diagonal
    pr[t,  : t - 1] = rep_vector(0, t - 1);
  }

  // Last column: probability of non-recapture
  for (t in 1 : n_occasions_minus_1) {
    pr[t, n_occasions] = 1 - sum(pr[t,  : n_occasions_minus_1]);
  }
}
model {
  // Priors
  phi ~ uniform(0, 1);
  p ~ uniform(0, 1);

  // Define the multinomial likelihood
  marr ~ multinomial(pr);
}
generated quantities {
  real fit;
  real fit_new;
  matrix[n_occasions_minus_1, n_occasions] E_org;
  matrix[n_occasions_minus_1, n_occasions] E_new;
  array[n_occasions_minus_1] vector[n_occasions] expmarr;
  array[n_occasions_minus_1, n_occasions] int<lower=0> marr_new;

  // Assess model fit using Freeman-Tukey statistic
  // Compute fit statistics for observed data
  for (t in 1 : n_occasions_minus_1) {
    expmarr[t] = r[t] * pr[t];
    for (j in 1 : n_occasions) {
      E_org[t, j] = square(sqrt(marr_safestan_copy[t][j]) - sqrt(expmarr[t][j]));
    } //j
  } //t

  // Generate replicate data and compute fit stats from them
  for (t in 1 : n_occasions_minus_1) {
    marr_new[t] = multinomial_rng(pr[t], r[t]);
    for (j in 1 : n_occasions) {
      E_new[t, j] = square(sqrt(marr_new[t][j]) - sqrt(expmarr[t][j]));
    }
  }
  fit = sum(E_org);
  fit_new = sum(E_new);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"marr":[[4,4,1],[4,2,3]],"n_occasions":3,"marr_safestan_copy":[[4,4,1],[4,2,3]]}","protected_variables":["marr"]}
